# Behold (CR 701.4a) is "choose a Dragon you control or reveal a Dragon card from your hand". Turn 3: Nova Hellkite is cast for
# its warp cost and is on the battlefield when Sarkhan enters, so the Dragon beheld is that permanent: it is chosen (the hand
# holds no Dragon card), nothing is revealed (`Bot1.Revealed` is absent), and the Treasure is created. The Hellkite had entered
# before Sarkhan, so there is no counter on him: he is a 2/2.

[Bot1 Deck]
Mountain
Mox Ruby
Mox Pearl
Mox Jet
Mox Sapphire
Sarkhan, Dragon Ascendant
Nova Hellkite
Island x12

[Bot2 Deck]
Island x15

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Mountain.Play
Bot1.Hand.Mox Ruby.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Pearl.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Jet.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Sapphire.Cast
[T3 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Battlefield.Mountain.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Pearl.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Jet.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Nova Hellkite.Cast(Ability: Warp)
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Ruby.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Sapphire.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Sarkhan, Dragon Ascendant.Cast
Bot1.Choose(Nova Hellkite)
[T3 Bot1.Main2]
? Bot1.Battlefield.Treasure Token.Token = true
? Bot1.Revealed = (absent)
? Bot1.Battlefield.Sarkhan, Dragon Ascendant.Power = 2

[Expect]
Bot1.Battlefield = Mountain; Mox Ruby; Mox Pearl; Mox Jet; Mox Sapphire; Sarkhan, Dragon Ascendant; Nova Hellkite; Treasure Token
Bot1.Revealed = (absent)
Bot1.Battlefield.Sarkhan, Dragon Ascendant.Power = 2
Bot1.Battlefield.Sarkhan, Dragon Ascendant.Toughness = 2
Bot1.Battlefield.Sarkhan, Dragon Ascendant.Subtypes = Druid; Human
